PART 3b | self-consistent closure  Q = b - g^2 Var(y^2|0 ; k=Q) : b=0 (pure YM) vs b>0
==============================================================================
     bare b=0.0 g=0.6 :  Q*=-0.39100  (residual 2.22e-16)   sign=NEGATIVE (no gap)
     bare b=0.0 g=1.0 :  Q*=-1.08611  (residual 8.88e-16)   sign=NEGATIVE (no gap)
     bare b=1.0 g=0.6 :  Q*= 0.78758  (residual 5.55e-16)   sign=POSITIVE source needed
     bare b=1.0 g=1.0 :  Q*=-0.08611  (residual 1.39e-17)   sign=NEGATIVE (no gap)

  READING:
   * b=0,g>0 (pure YM): the self-consistent curvature is Q*<=0 (Savvidy/unstable sign).
     There is NO positive fixed point -- the fixpoint does not GENERATE a scale.
   * b>0: Q*>0 because the BARE MASS b is the source. Pure YM has no such bare mass.
   * the free massless fixpoint is exactly Q=0.  => Q=0 is admissible; no source at Q=0. [V-here]

