SUMMARY (no QED)
==============================================================================
 1 pointwise: PSD minorant of an indefinite Hessian does NOT exist (Savvidy kills it). [T]
 2 expectation: E[Hess]=E[f^2]>=0 by Stein -- true, but gap-blind (free field saturates). [T]
 3 fixpoint Q=G''(0): Q=0 admissible (free); pure YM (b=0) => Q*<=0, NO source at Q=0. [V-here]
 4 uniformity: the positive branch needs spontaneous scale breaking = the gap (=H1).
 => The quadratic-minorant fixpoint does NOT exclude the gapless point; Q=0 solves it,
    there is no source at Q=0, and a nonzero fixed point IS dimensional transmutation. NO QED.
